      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 78-year-old patient with prostate cancer and osseous metastases had a pain symptomatic. In the Urology he was treated with antiandrogenes. The outcome of the bone scintigraphy showed a super bone scan with normalization after antiandrogene-therapy which seemed to be a sign of remission, before he showed a progressive form with multiple osseous metastases. Pain could not be treated with non steroidal antiphlogistics and opiates, so the indication for treatment with Rhenium-186-HEDP was given in this case."},
